==============================================================================================================
TEST A -- CREEP ONLY.  Is the law eps_dot = A sigma^n when there is no yield surface?
==============================================================================================================
  Two ways to remove the yield surface are probed, because they are NOT equivalent:
    'none' = omit *PLASTIC entirely.  materialdata_me.f sets plconloc(801)=0.5, so
             incplas.f:130 takes user_hardening=1 and calls uhardening(), whose
             default body (src/uhardening.f) is an empty RETURN -- it never assigns
             fiso, which incplas.f never initialises.  The yield stress is then
             whatever was left on the stack.  This is undefined behaviour.
    'zero' = keep *PLASTIC but set sigma_y = 1e-6 MPa, flat.  user_hardening stays 0
             and the overstress equals sigma_vm to 7 significant figures.

